    <!--
        The Web OAuth client ID, read by the Google Sign-In SDK on Android.

        Not the Android client ID, and that distinction is the whole trick. The
        Android client authorises this app: Google matches it on package name
        and signing certificate, it holds no secret, and it is never named
        anywhere in code or config. What Supabase will accept is a token issued
        for its own client, so Google is asked for one addressed to the web
        client and hands it to an app already proven to be ours.

        Public by design. An OAuth client ID is not a credential, and this same
        value already ships inside the JavaScript bundle.
